{
  "step_1": "The decision reason focuses on comparing probabilities between the two lotteries, particularly the probability of obtaining a favorable outcome, and prefers the lottery with the higher probability of such an outcome. In this decision problem, Lottery A offers a 50% chance of winning 1000 Euros and a 50% chance of winning 0 Euros, while Lottery B offers a 100% chance of winning 500 Euros. A favorable outcome can reasonably be interpreted as receiving a positive monetary gain. Both lotteries provide a positive outcome with at least 50% (A) or 100% (B) probability. The relevant information for the decision reason is thus the probability of a non-zero outcome: 50% for A and 100% for B. Since B has a higher probability of yielding a favorable (non-zero) outcome, the decision reason would prefer Lottery B.",
