{
  "step_1": "The decision reason focuses on comparing the probabilities of obtaining a favorable outcome between the two lotteries, preferring the one with the higher probability of a favorable outcome. A 'favorable outcome' is not explicitly defined, but given the context of monetary lotteries, it can be interpreted as receiving a positive (non-zero) monetary outcome. For Lottery A: probability of a favorable outcome (i.e., winning 6000 Euros) is 25%. For Lottery B: probability of a favorable outcome is 25% (4000 Euros) + 25% (2000 Euros) = 50%. Thus, Lottery B has a higher probability of a favorable outcome. The decision reason would therefore prefer Lottery B. The relevant information (probabilities of non-zero outcomes) can be derived from the problem, so the reason is applicable.",
