{
  "step_1": "The decision reason focuses on comparing the probabilities of the two lotteries, particularly emphasizing the probability of a favorable outcome. A 'favorable outcome' must be defined in context. Given that all outcomes involve zero or negative amounts (i.e., no gains), a 'favorable outcome' likely means the least negative outcome, which is 0 Euros. Lottery A offers 0 Euros with 75% probability. Lottery B offers 0 Euros with 50% probability. Thus, Lottery A has a higher probability of the favorable outcome (0 Euros). The reason would prefer Lottery A. The relevant information (probabilities of favorable outcomes) can be derived from the lotteries, so the reason is applicable.",
